  'LFU': 'LFU evicts the least frequently accessed entry, usually with aging so historical popularity does not dominate forever.',
  'Cache Penetration': 'Cache penetration repeatedly requests nonexistent keys that miss cache and hit storage; negative caching and validation mitigate it.',
  'Cache Avalanche': 'A cache avalanche is a large simultaneous expiry or cache outage that shifts excessive load to the origin.',
  'Distributed Cache': 'A distributed cache is shared across application instances and adds network, partitioning, and serialization costs.',
  'Local Cache': 'A local in-process cache has very low latency but duplicates memory and can diverge across instances.',
  'CDN Cache': 'A CDN cache stores HTTP responses at edge locations close to clients.',
  'Browser Cache': 'A browser cache privately reuses responses according to HTTP freshness and validation rules.',
  'HTTP Cache': 'An HTTP cache is a browser or intermediary that stores reusable responses under standard cache-control semantics.',
  'Cache Versioning': 'Cache versioning changes a key namespace when representation or source semantics change, making old entries unreachable.',
  'Memcached': 'Memcached is a distributed in-memory key/value cache with simple expiration and no built-in persistence or replication.',
  'Cloudflare CDN': 'Cloudflare CDN caches and proxies HTTP traffic through edge locations with configurable cache, security, and routing policies.',
  'Topics': 'A broker topic is a named logical stream to which producers publish and consumers subscribe.',
  'Partitions': 'A messaging partition is an ordered shard of a topic and the main unit of consumer parallelism.',
  'Brokers': 'A message broker accepts, stores or routes, and delivers messages between producers and consumers.',
  'Producers': 'A producer publishes records with payload, metadata, and often a partition or routing key.',
  'Consumers': 'A consumer polls or receives messages, performs side effects, and acknowledges or commits progress.',
  'Offsets': 'An offset identifies a record position in an ordered partition and is separate from processing success.',
  'Partition Ordering': 'Partition ordering guarantees records are observed in log order only within one partition.',
  'Retention': 'Retention removes old records according to time or size regardless of whether every consumer read them.',
  'Log Compaction': 'Kafka log compaction retains the latest record per key, plus tombstone behavior, rather than a complete event history.',
  'At-Most-Once Delivery': 'At-most-once delivery may lose work but never intentionally retries after uncertain processing.',
  'Exactly-Once Semantics': 'Kafka exactly-once semantics atomically commits produced records and consumed offsets within Kafka transactions, not arbitrary external side effects.',
  'Consumer Rebalancing': 'A rebalance revokes and reassigns partitions among group members, temporarily pausing or moving ownership.',
  'Kafka Connect': 'Kafka Connect runs reusable source and sink connectors with distributed task management and offset storage.',
  'Kafka Streams': 'Kafka Streams is a JVM library for stateful event processing with partitions, local state stores, changelogs, and exactly-once modes.',
  'Exchanges': 'A RabbitMQ exchange routes published messages to queues according to its type, bindings, and routing key.',
  'Bindings': 'A binding connects a RabbitMQ exchange to a queue or another exchange with routing criteria.',
