  'Partition Tolerance': 'Partition tolerance means the system continues with a defined behavior despite lost or delayed messages between node groups.',
  'Clock Synchronization': 'Clock synchronization estimates wall time across machines but cannot remove skew, drift, or network-delay uncertainty.',
  'Database Sharding': 'Database sharding places disjoint rows on separate database nodes using a shard key.',
  'Database Scaling': 'Database scaling combines query tuning, indexes, pooling, replicas, partitioning, sharding, and workload separation.',
  'CDN': 'A CDN serves cacheable content through geographically distributed edge nodes to reduce origin load and user latency.',
